.TH P3M-LS 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-ls \- parallel recursive directory lister
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-ls
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-ls
walks one or more directory trees with a pool of worker threads and emits
every entry found as CSV.
It is a high-performance alternative to
.BR "ls \-R" " and " find (1)
for cataloguing large trees, and is fastest on directories with very many
entries and on storage where each metadata operation has latency (NFS, CIFS,
cluster file systems).
.PP
With no
.IR PATH ,
the current directory is scanned.
Multiple paths are scanned concurrently as part of the same run.
The root paths themselves are not emitted, only their contents.
.PP
Output row order is non-deterministic because directories are processed in
parallel; pipe through
.BR sort (1)
if a stable order is required.
Symbolic links are reported but never followed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fILEVEL\fR"
Detail level:
.BR basic " (default), " standard " or " full .
Single-letter abbreviations are accepted.
See
.BR "DETAIL LEVELS" .
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Number of worker threads, 1\(en512.
Default: the number of online CPUs.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " \fITYPES\fR"
Only output entries of the given types.
Types combine freely, for example
.BR "\-t fl" .
See
.BR "TYPE CHARACTERS" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dirs
Omit directories from the output.
The walk still descends into them.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the CSV to
.I FILE
instead of standard output, and show a live progress display on the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing.
Progress (on a terminal) and the end-of-run summary are still shown, and a
.B \-o
file is still written in full.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH DETAIL LEVELS
.TP
.B basic
One column,
.IR path .
Entries are classified from the directory stream and normally no
.BR stat (2)
calls are issued at all.
.TP
.B standard
.nf
path,type,size,mode,owner,group,mtime
.fi
.TP
.B full
Every field
.BR stat (2)
provides:
.nf
path,type,mode,perms,nlink,owner,uid,group,gid,size,
blksize,blocks,dev,ino,rdev,atime,mtime,ctime
.fi
.IP
.IR atime ,
.I mtime
and
.I ctime
are ISO\ 8601 UTC with nanosecond precision.
This is the input format expected by
.BR p3m\-stats (1).
.SH TYPE CHARACTERS
.TS
l l.
f	regular file
d	directory
l	symbolic link
b	block device
c	character device
p	FIFO (named pipe)
s	socket
.TE
.PP
.B \-t
values may be concatenated, are case-insensitive, and may use an optional
comma separator.
.SH CSV FORMAT
The first line is always a header row.
Fields containing commas, double quotes or newlines are quoted per RFC\ 4180,
so the output loads directly into spreadsheets,
.BR sqlite3 (1)
.BR .import ,
pandas, and similar tools.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Completed, but errors were encountered (or the output could not be fully written).
.TP
.B 2
Usage or startup error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fast inventory of a tree, one path per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-ls /data
.fi
.RE
.PP
Full metadata catalogue written to a file, with live progress:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-ls \-m full \-o catalogue.csv /data
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only symlinks and regular files, 16 threads (high-latency NFS):
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-ls \-j 16 \-t fl \-\-no\-dirs \-m standard /mnt/nfs/share
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-stats (1),
.BR p3m\-find (1),
.BR p3m\-du (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR ls (1)
